# Project: risk-based authentication (RBA) — PFI thesis

Solo final project. Goal: a transparent, explainable login-risk scorer, ultimately
deployed as polyrepo microservices on Kubernetes. Org: `github.com/roku-pfi`.

## Workspace repos (each a separate git repo, cloned side-by-side)

- `rba-features` — shared feature library. The ONE implementation of every feature,
  imported by both offline training and (later) online scoring.
- `rba-ml-training` — offline data + modelling pipeline (ingest, EDA, train, evaluate).
- `docs` — devlog, ADRs (`decisions/`), findings, and the plan (`plans/`).

## Current status

**Single source of truth: `docs/plans/status.md`** (phase/step checklist + current
focus). Phase rationale: `docs/plans/development_plan.md` §8.

Phase 1 (data + model feasibility) is **complete**: Steps 1–6 done (env, subset
builder, EDA, feature library, Freeman scorer + baselines, `is_attack_ip` leakage A/B)
plus a Freeman calibration pass (β 10→5). **Next: Phase 2 — freeze the
feature/model/scoring + `/risk/evaluate` contracts.** Infra (Docker/k8s/Helm/Argo) is
later phases, not now.

## Stack (decided — see docs/decisions/)

Python 3.12 + FastAPI backend; React/TS + Vite frontend; PostgreSQL + Redis +
RabbitMQ; LightGBM/XGBoost/scikit-learn/SHAP + MLflow; Docker/Kubernetes/Helm/Argo;
Prometheus + Grafana. Dev on an M2 Pro Mac; venv at `rba-ml-training/.venv`.

Before non-trivial work, skim `docs/plans/status.md` (where we are), `docs/decisions/`
(ADRs), and the latest `docs/devlog.md` entry for current context.
